# Site component conventions

## Content is typed data, not JSX

Essays live in `src/lib/essays.ts`, FAQs in `src/lib/faqs.ts`, audit questions in
`src/lib/audit.ts`, builds in `src/lib/builds.ts`, site constants in
`src/lib/site.ts`. These feed pages, `sitemap.ts`, `feed.xml`, `llms.txt`, OG
images, and JSON-LD. Add content there, never inline in a component, and update
`llms.txt` when offers or essays change.

`MAX_SCORE` in `audit.ts` is derived (`AUDIT.length * 2`). If you change the
question count, the verdict ranges and every copy reference to "ten questions"
must move with it.

## The lamp is the site's identity

`components/hero.tsx` (dark room + pull cord), `components/overture.tsx` (opt-in
three-beat opening), `src/lib/overture-gate.ts` (`revealPage`/`onReveal`,
`requestOverture`/`onOvertureRequest`), and `app/not-found.tsx` (unlit 404) share
one metaphor: the visitor turns the light on. Keep the bulb SVG, brass glow, and
cord physics consistent if you touch any of them. The Overture must stay opt-in;
it must never gate first paint again.

## Known traps

- `whileInView` on a mask-clipped child never fires. Hoist the trigger to an
  unclipped ancestor and drive children with variants.
- Never add `position` to a sticky host.
- Keep `[data-torch]` rules unlayered in `globals.css`.
- In `next/og` (satori), a `div` with more than one child needs explicit
  `display: flex`, and text interpolations must be a single template string.
- Use `svh` fallbacks via `@supports not (height: 100svh)`; duplicate
  declarations get stripped by the minifier.

## Accessibility floor

Touch targets ≥44px, visible focus states, real SVG icons (lucide) never emoji,
accessible labels on icon-only controls and decorative-but-meaningful graphics,
and contrast that holds on both ink and bone grounds.
